% Nebulizers: LCD L33370 and its Policy Article A52466 (DME MACs). A policy
% program of the DMEPOS model: it includes dmepos.le (orders, delivery,
% benefit category, continued need, refills) and states when a claim for a
% nebulizer compressor (the small volume nebulizer compressor E0570, the
% aerosol compressors E0565 and E0572, the ultrasonic generator E0574, the
% combination system E0585, the durable bottle nebulizer E0580 used with an
% oxygen system), an accessory (the small volume nebulizers A7003–A7005, the
% filtered nebulizer A7006, the large volume nebulizers A7007 and A7017, the
% filters, tubing, masks and heater of the LCD's accessory table), an
% inhalation drug (the J codes) or the water and saline used with them
% (A4216, A4217, A4218, A7018) is REASONABLE AND NECESSARY: the drug is
% covered for the diagnosis the record states (the ICD-10 groups of the
% Policy Article), the equipment administers a covered drug or delivers
% humidity for thick tenacious secretions, the accessory belongs to a
% covered compressor, the quantities are within the usual maximum per month
% and the usual maximum replacement, and no drug is billed together with a
% drug the LCD excludes it with. A large volume ultrasonic nebulizer (E0575)
% and a compounded inhalation solution are never covered: no rule concludes
% them. The battery-powered compressor E0571 is named by neither text: it is
% among the policy's codes and no rule covers it.
%
% How the criteria are read. The LCD says a drug is reasonable and necessary
% for a condition and refers to the Policy Article's ICD-10 groups for the
% diagnoses; the article's table is data (sources/icd10/A52466_icd10_covered.csv,
% loaded as the table nebulizer_icd10), the claim's diagnosis code a record
% fact. The article's text file does not carry the "Group N" paragraphs, so
% the groups are mapped to codes from the LCD's own cross-references:
%   group 1  — E0565 or E0572 compressor with the filtered nebulizer A7006
%              (pentamidine: the union of the groups 4 and 5 in the table);
%   group 3  — the small volume nebulizer A7003, A7004, A7005 and E0570
%              (the union of the drug groups; not read: the drugs decide);
%   group 4  — pentamidine J2545;
%   group 5  — the large volume nebulizer A7007, A7017, E0585, the
%              compressor E0565 or E0572, water or saline A4217, A7018 (and
%              E0580, the same equipment as A7017 per the article);
%   group 7  — acetylcysteine J7608;
%   group 8  — albuterol J7611, J7613, arformoterol J7605, budesonide J7626,
%              cromolyn J7631, formoterol J7606, ipratropium J7644,
%              levalbuterol J7612, J7614, metaproterenol J7669, revefenacin J7677;
%   group 9  — dornase alfa J7639;
%   group 10 — tobramycin J7682;
%   group 11 — E0574 and treprostinil J7686;
%   group 14 — K0730 and iloprost Q4074 (not modelled);
%   group 15 — hypertonic saline J7131;
%   group 16 — ensifentrine J7601.
%   Groups 2, 6, 12 and 13 are not referenced by the LCD and are not read.
% The findings this policy reads (dmepos.le's judged template), and the
% criterion each stands for:
%   maintenance therapy insufficient (ensifentrine: continued COPD
%   exacerbations or persistent dyspnea despite dual or triple maintenance
%   therapy); qualifying pulmonary hypertension etiology (treprostinil
%   criteria 2 and 3: not secondary to pulmonary venous hypertension or a
%   respiratory disorder, and primary or secondary to connective tissue
%   disease, HIV, cirrhosis, anorexigens or a congenital shunt); pulmonary
%   hypertension progressed despite treatment (criterion 3.a); significant
%   pulmonary hypertension symptoms (criteria 3.c and 4.e); calcium channel
%   blockers excluded (criterion 3.d: tried and failed, or ruled out).
% What the record states as fact — the diagnosis code, the drug a device
% administers, the other drugs furnished to the beneficiary, the maintenance
% therapy, the pressures and the resistance, the CT confirmation, the thick
% tenacious secretions — is a scenario fact. The dispensing fees, the
% modifiers, the licensing of the dispensing entity and the room
% humidification exclusion of the article are not modelled.
%
% The payment conditions the policy adds (Policy Article A52466, LCD "Refill
% requirements"): no more than a three-month quantity of a supply at a time;
% for ensifentrine, the practitioner documents the continued maintenance
% therapy and the exacerbations or the dyspnea; E0580 only with a
% beneficiary-owned oxygen system.

the target language is: prolog.

the templates are:
    % the record
    *a drug* is administered with *a device*; undefined.
    the maintenance therapy of *a beneficiary* is *a therapy*; undefined.
    *an item* is used with a patient owned oxygen system; undefined.
    the mean pulmonary artery pressure of *a beneficiary* at rest is *a number* mm Hg; undefined.
    the mean pulmonary artery pressure of *a beneficiary* with exertion is *a number* mm Hg; undefined.
    the pulmonary capillary wedge pressure of *a beneficiary* is *a number* mm Hg; undefined.
    the left ventricular end-diastolic pressure of *a beneficiary* is *a number* mm Hg; undefined.
    the pulmonary vascular resistance of *a beneficiary* at rest is *a number* Wood units; undefined.
    interstitial lung disease of *a beneficiary* was confirmed by a high-resolution CT scan of the chest; undefined.
    % the tables
    ICD10 code *a code* is in group *a group* of article *an article* as *a description* under table nebulizer_icd10.
    the usual maximum for code *a code* of drug *a drug* is *a quantity* units per month under table nebulizer_drug_max.
    the rescue maximum for code *a code* is *a quantity* units per month under table nebulizer_rescue_max.
    the related compressor of accessory *a code* is *an other code* under table nebulizer_related.
    the usual maximum replacement for accessory *a code* is *a quantity* under table nebulizer_accessory_quantity.
    the period of the usual maximum replacement for accessory *a code* is *a number* months under table nebulizer_accessory_period.
    % derived
    *an item* is nebulizer equipment.
    *an item* is a nebulizer accessory.
    *an item* is an inhalation drug.
    *an item* is a nebulizer supply.
    *a drug* is a small volume nebulizer drug.
    the diagnosis of *a beneficiary* is in ICD10 group *a group*.
    *an item* is a covered inhalation drug for *a beneficiary*.
    *a beneficiary* meets the ensifentrine criteria.
    *a beneficiary* meets the pulmonary arterial hypertension criteria.
    *a beneficiary* meets the interstitial lung disease criteria.
    the mean pulmonary artery pressure of *a beneficiary* is elevated.
    the filling pressure of *a beneficiary* is low.
    *a beneficiary* meets the humidification criteria.
    *a device* administers a covered small volume nebulizer drug.
    *a device* administers covered pentamidine.
    *a device* administers covered treprostinil.
    *a device* meets the nebulizer coverage criteria.
    *an item* conflicts with a concurrent inhalation drug.
    *an item* is a rescue medication for *a beneficiary*.
    *a claim* is within the usual maximum quantity per month.
    *a claim* is within the usual maximum replacement of the accessory.
    the ensifentrine documentation requirements are met for *a claim*.

% The Policy Article's ICD-10 table: the covered codes of each group. The
% file read is a copy of sources/icd10/A52466_icd10_covered.csv in which the
% word "and" of a description is written "&": the table loader reads a cell
% holding "and" as a condition and drops the row (144 rows, 21 codes — among
% them I27.23, J44.81, J68.x, J69.x and the T86.9x transplant complications
% — would be lost). Point the table back at the original once the loader
% accepts the word in a value cell.
the table nebulizer_icd10 is loaded from sources/icd10/A52466_icd10_covered.csv, with all matches:
    code | group | article | description

% The maximum per month of each inhalation drug and solution (LCD L33370,
% "INHALATION DRUGS AND SOLUTIONS"), in the billing unit of the code: 1 mg of
% albuterol (J7611, J7613), 0.5 mg of levalbuterol (J7612, J7614), 10 mg of
% metaproterenol (J7669) and of cromolyn (J7631), 1 mg of ipratropium
% (J7644), 1 g of acetylcysteine (J7608), 300 mg of pentamidine (J2545), 1 ml
% of hypertonic saline (J7131), 1 mcg of revefenacin (J7677); water or saline
% for the large volume nebulizer is 18 liters a month, 36 units of 500 ml
% (A4217) or 18 units of 1000 ml (A7018).
the table nebulizer_drug_max is, with unique match, with provenance LCD L33370,
        confer "The following table represents the maximum per month of inhalation drugs that are reasonable and necessary for each nebulizer drug":
    code    | drug                              | units | confer
    "J7608" | acetylcysteine                    | 74    | "Acetylcysteine 74 grams/month"
    "J7611" | albuterol                         | 465   | "Albuterol 465 mg/month"
    "J7613" | albuterol                         | 465   | "Albuterol 465 mg/month"
    "J7620" | albuterol ipratropium combination | 186   | "Albuterol/Ipratropium combination 186 units/month"
    "J7605" | arformoterol                      | 62    | "Arformoterol 930 micrograms/month – 62 units/month"
    "J7626" | budesonide                        | 62    | "Budesonide 62 units/month"
    "J7631" | cromolyn                          | 248   | "Cromolyn sodium 2480 mg/month – 248 units/month"
    "J7639" | dornase alfa                      | 78    | "Dornase alfa 78 mg/month"
    "J7601" | ensifentrine                      | 60    | "Ensifentrine 180 mg/month – 60 units/month"
    "J7606" | formoterol                        | 62    | "Formoterol 1240 micrograms/month – 62 units/month"
    "J7131" | hypertonic saline                 | 240   | "Hypertonic Saline 240 ml/month"
    "J7644" | ipratropium                       | 93    | "Ipratropium bromide 93 mg/month"
    "J7612" | levalbuterol                      | 465   | "Levalbuterol 232.5 mg/month – 465 units/month"
    "J7614" | levalbuterol                      | 465   | "Levalbuterol 232.5 mg/month – 465 units/month"
    "J7669" | metaproterenol                    | 280   | "Metaproterenol 2800 mg/month – 280 units/month"
    "J2545" | pentamidine                       | 1     | "Pentamidine 300 mg/month"
    "J7677" | revefenacin                       | 5250  | "Revefenacin 5250 mcg/month"
    "J7686" | treprostinil                      | 31    | "Treprostinil 31 units/month"
    "A4216" | sterile saline                    | 56    | "Sterile saline or water, 10ml/unit (A4216, A4218) 56 units/month"
    "A4218" | sterile saline                    | 56    | "Sterile saline or water, 10ml/unit (A4216, A4218) 56 units/month"
    "A4217" | water                             | 36    | "Distilled water, sterile water, or sterile saline in large volume nebulizer 18 liters/month"
    "A7018" | water                             | 18    | "Distilled water, sterile water, or sterile saline in large volume nebulizer 18 liters/month"

% The maximum per month of a short-acting bronchodilator used as a rescue
% medication beside formoterol or arformoterol (the same units).
the table nebulizer_rescue_max is, with unique match, with provenance LCD L33370,
        confer "When albuterol, levalbuterol, or metaproterenol are prescribed as rescue/supplemental medication for beneficiaries who are taking formoterol or arformoterol, the maximum per month that are reasonably billed are":
    code    | units | confer
    "J7611" | 78    | "Albuterol 78 mg/month"
    "J7613" | 78    | "Albuterol 78 mg/month"
    "J7620" | 31    | "Albuterol/Ipratropium combination 31 units/month"
    "J7612" | 78    | "Levalbuterol 39 mg/month – 78 units/month"
    "J7614" | 78    | "Levalbuterol 39 mg/month – 78 units/month"
    "J7669" | 47    | "Metaproterenol 470 mg/month – 47 units/month"

% The compressor or generator each accessory is related to (LCD L33370,
% "ACCESSORIES"); K0730 is not modelled.
the table nebulizer_related is, with all matches, with provenance LCD L33370,
        confer "The following table lists the compressor/generator, which is related to the accessories described":
    accessory | compressor | confer
    "A4619" or "A7006" or "A7007" or "A7010" or "A7012" or "A7013" or "A7014" or "A7015" or "A7017" or "A7525" or "E1372" | "E0565" | "E0565 A4619, A7006, A7007, A7010, A7012, A7013, A7014, A7015, A7017, A7525, E1372"
    "A7003" or "A7004" or "A7005" or "A7006" or "A7013" or "A7015" or "A7525" | "E0570" | "E0570 A7003, A7004, A7005, A7006, A7013, A7015, A7525"
    "A7006" or "A7007" or "A7014" or "A7017" | "E0572" | "E0572 A7006, A7007, A7014, A7017"
    "A7013" or "A7014" or "A7016" | "E0574" | "E0574 A7013, A7014, A7016"
    "A4619" or "A7006" or "A7010" or "A7012" or "A7013" or "A7014" or "A7015" or "A7525" | "E0585" | "E0585 A4619, A7006, A7010, A7012, A7013, A7014, A7015, A7525"

% The usual maximum replacement of each accessory: a quantity per period
% (a year is 12 months, three years 36).
the table nebulizer_accessory_quantity is, with unique match, with provenance LCD L33370,
        confer "The following table lists the usual maximum frequency of replacement for accessories":
    code    | quantity | confer
    "A4619" | 1        | "A4619 One/month"
    "A7003" | 2        | "A7003 Two/month"
    "A7004" | 2        | "A7004 Two/month"
    "A7005" | 1        | "A7005 One/6 months"
    "A7006" | 1        | "A7006 One/month"
    "A7007" | 2        | "A7007 Two/month"
    "A7010" | 1        | "A7010 One unit (100 ft.)/2 months"
    "A7012" | 2        | "A7012 Two/month"
    "A7013" | 2        | "A7013 Two/month"
    "A7014" | 1        | "A7014 One/3 months"
    "A7015" | 1        | "A7015 One/month"
    "A7016" | 2        | "A7016 Two/year"
    "A7017" | 1        | "A7017 One/3 years"
    "A7525" | 1        | "A7525 One/month"
    "E1372" | 1        | "E1372 One/3 years"

the table nebulizer_accessory_period is, with unique match, with provenance LCD L33370,
        confer "The following table lists the usual maximum frequency of replacement for accessories":
    code    | months | confer
    "A4619" | 1      | "A4619 One/month"
    "A7003" | 1      | "A7003 Two/month"
    "A7004" | 1      | "A7004 Two/month"
    "A7005" | 6      | "A7005 One/6 months"
    "A7006" | 1      | "A7006 One/month"
    "A7007" | 1      | "A7007 Two/month"
    "A7010" | 2      | "A7010 One unit (100 ft.)/2 months"
    "A7012" | 1      | "A7012 Two/month"
    "A7013" | 1      | "A7013 Two/month"
    "A7014" | 3      | "A7014 One/3 months"
    "A7015" | 1      | "A7015 One/month"
    "A7016" | 12     | "A7016 Two/year"
    "A7017" | 36     | "A7017 One/3 years"
    "A7525" | 1      | "A7525 One/month"
    "E1372" | 36     | "E1372 One/3 years"

the knowledge base nebulizers includes these resources:
    dmepos.

the knowledge base nebulizers includes:

LCD L33370 is published at "https://www.cms.gov/medicare-coverage-database/view/lcd.aspx?lcdid=33370".
the text of LCD L33370 is at "sources/lcd/L33370.txt".
Policy Article A52466 is published at "https://www.cms.gov/medicare-coverage-database/view/article.aspx?articleid=52466".
the text of Policy Article A52466 is at "sources/article/A52466.txt".

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% What the items are: equipment, accessories, drugs, supplies.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

rule neb_equipment with provenance Policy Article A52466,
        confer "In this policy, nebulization of inhalation solutions is accomplished by two types of devices":
an item is nebulizer equipment
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["E0565", "E0570", "E0571", "E0572", "E0574", "E0575", "E0580", "E0585"].

rule neb_accessory with provenance LCD L33370,
        confer "Accessories are separately payable if the related aerosol compressor and the individual accessories are reasonable and necessary":
an item is a nebulizer accessory
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["A4619", "A7003", "A7004", "A7005", "A7006", "A7007", "A7010", "A7012", "A7013", "A7014", "A7015", "A7016", "A7017", "A7525", "E1372"].

rule neb_inhalation_drug with provenance LCD L33370,
        confer "Such supplies include those drugs and biologicals which must be put directly into the equipment in order to achieve the therapeutic benefit of the durable medical equipment":
an item is an inhalation drug
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["J2545", "J7131", "J7601", "J7605", "J7606", "J7608", "J7611", "J7612", "J7613", "J7614", "J7620", "J7626", "J7631", "J7639", "J7644", "J7669", "J7677", "J7682", "J7686"].

% A supply: a drug, a solution or an accessory, provided on a recurring
% basis — a device of this model, for the dispensing limit.
rule neb_supply_drug:
an item is a nebulizer supply
    if the item is an inhalation drug.

rule neb_supply_accessory:
an item is a nebulizer supply
    if the item is a nebulizer accessory.

rule neb_supply_solution:
an item is a nebulizer supply
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["A4216", "A4217", "A4218", "A7018"].

% The drugs a small volume nebulizer and its compressor (E0570) are covered
% to administer.
rule neb_small_volume_drugs with provenance LCD L33370,
        confer "A small volume nebulizer (A7003, A7004, A7005), and related compressor (E0570) are considered for coverage when it is reasonable and necessary to administer the following FDA-approved inhalation solutions listed below":
a drug is a small volume nebulizer drug
    if the HCPCS code of the drug is a code
    and the code is in ["J7611", "J7613", "J7605", "J7626", "J7631", "J7606", "J7644", "J7612", "J7614", "J7669", "J7677", "J7639", "J7682", "J2545", "J7608", "J7131", "J7601"].

% The diagnosis of the claim, read against the article's table.
rule neb_diagnosis_group with provenance Policy Article A52466,
        confer "A diagnosis code describing the condition which necessitates nebulizer therapy must be included on each claim for equipment, accessories, and/or drugs":
the diagnosis of a beneficiary is in ICD10 group a group
    if the diagnosis code of the beneficiary is a code
    and ICD10 code the code is in group the group of article "A52466" as a description under table nebulizer_icd10.

% The codes this policy decides — outside the section checklist: a claim
% of another policy fails here without failing its own applicability.
% The codes this policy decides — the equipment, the accessories, the water
% and saline, the FDA-approved drugs and the compounded solutions the LCD
% denies — and their benefit: durable medical equipment and the supplies
% necessary for its effective use (Policy Article A52466).
rule neb_codes_equipment with provenance Policy Article A52466,
        confer "Nebulizers are covered under the Durable Medical Equipment (DME) benefit":
the policy for code a code is nebulizers
    if the code is in ["E0565", "E0570", "E0571", "E0572", "E0574", "E0575", "E0580", "E0585", "A4619", "A7003", "A7004", "A7005", "A7006", "A7007", "A7010", "A7012", "A7013", "A7014", "A7015", "A7016", "A7017", "A7525", "E1372", "A4216", "A4217", "A4218", "A7018"].

rule neb_codes_drugs with provenance LCD L33370,
        confer "Payment may be made for supplies that are necessary for the effective use of durable medical equipment":
the policy for code a code is nebulizers
    if the code is in ["J2545", "J7131", "J7601", "J7605", "J7606", "J7608", "J7611", "J7612", "J7613", "J7614", "J7620", "J7626", "J7631", "J7639", "J7644", "J7669", "J7677", "J7682", "J7686"].

rule neb_codes_compounded with provenance LCD L33370,
        confer "Compounded inhalation solutions (J7604, J7607, J7609, J7610, J7615, J7622, J7624, J7627, J7628, J7629, J7632, J7634, J7635, J7636, J7637, J7638, J7640, J7641, J7642, J7643, J7645, J7647, J7650, J7657, J7660, J7667, J7670, J7676, J7680, J7681, J7683, J7684, J7685, and compounded solutions billed with J7699) will be denied as not reasonable and necessary":
the policy for code a code is nebulizers
    if the code is in ["J7604", "J7607", "J7609", "J7610", "J7615", "J7622", "J7624", "J7627", "J7628", "J7629", "J7632", "J7634", "J7635", "J7636", "J7637", "J7638", "J7640", "J7641", "J7642", "J7643", "J7645", "J7647", "J7650", "J7657", "J7660", "J7667", "J7670", "J7676", "J7680", "J7681", "J7683", "J7684", "J7685", "J7699"].

section applicability is:

rule neb_benefit with provenance Policy Article A52466,
        confer "Nebulizers are covered under the Durable Medical Equipment (DME) benefit":
the benefit category of code a code is durable medical equipment
    if the policy for code the code is nebulizers.

section question is:

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% The equipment: covered when it administers a covered drug, or delivers
% humidity for thick tenacious secretions.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

rule neb_equipment_claim with provenance LCD L33370,
        confer "If none of the drugs used with a nebulizer are covered, the compressor, the nebulizer, and other related accessories/supplies will be denied as not reasonable and necessary":
a claim is reasonable and necessary
    if the claim is for an item
    and the item is nebulizer equipment
    and the item meets the nebulizer coverage criteria.

rule neb_small_volume_compressor with provenance LCD L33370,
        confer "A small volume nebulizer (A7003, A7004, A7005), and related compressor (E0570) are considered for coverage when it is reasonable and necessary to administer the following FDA-approved inhalation solutions listed below":
a device meets the nebulizer coverage criteria
    if the HCPCS code of the device is "E0570"
    and the device administers a covered small volume nebulizer drug.

rule neb_administers_small_volume_drug with provenance LCD L33370,
        confer "If none of the drugs used with a nebulizer are covered, the compressor, the nebulizer, and other related accessories/supplies will be denied as not reasonable and necessary":
a device administers a covered small volume nebulizer drug
    if the device is furnished to a beneficiary
    and a drug is administered with the device
    and the drug is a small volume nebulizer drug
    and the drug is a covered inhalation drug for the beneficiary.

rule neb_pentamidine_compressor with provenance LCD L33370,
        confer "it is reasonable and necessary to administer pentamidine to beneficiaries with HIV, pneumocystosis, or complications of organ transplants (refer to the Group 1 Codes in the LCD-related Policy Article for applicable diagnoses)":
a device meets the nebulizer coverage criteria
    if the HCPCS code of the device is a code
    and the code is in ["E0565", "E0572"]
    and the device administers covered pentamidine.

rule neb_administers_pentamidine with provenance LCD L33370,
        confer "An E0565 or E0572 compressor and filtered nebulizer (A7006)":
a device administers covered pentamidine
    if the device is furnished to a beneficiary
    and a drug is administered with the device
    and the HCPCS code of the drug is "J2545"
    and the drug is a covered inhalation drug for the beneficiary.

rule neb_large_volume_compressor with provenance LCD L33370,
        confer "A large volume nebulizer (A7007, A7017), related compressor (E0565 or E0572), and water or saline (A4217 or A7018) are considered for coverage when it is reasonable and necessary to deliver humidity to a beneficiary with thick, tenacious secretions, who has cystic fibrosis, bronchiectasis, a tracheostomy, or a tracheobronchial stent":
a device meets the nebulizer coverage criteria
    if the HCPCS code of the device is a code
    and the code is in ["E0565", "E0572"]
    and the device is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the beneficiary meets the humidification criteria.

rule neb_combination_system with provenance LCD L33370,
        confer "Combination code E0585 will be covered for the same indications":
a device meets the nebulizer coverage criteria
    if the HCPCS code of the device is "E0585"
    and the device is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the beneficiary meets the humidification criteria.

rule neb_bottle_nebulizer with provenance Policy Article A52466,
        confer "describes the same piece of equipment as A7017, but should only be billed when this type of nebulizer is used with a beneficiary-owned oxygen system":
a device meets the nebulizer coverage criteria
    if the HCPCS code of the device is "E0580"
    and the device is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the beneficiary meets the humidification criteria.

rule neb_humidification with provenance LCD L33370,
        confer "reasonable and necessary to deliver humidity to a beneficiary with thick, tenacious secretions, who has cystic fibrosis, bronchiectasis, a tracheostomy, or a tracheobronchial stent (refer to the Group 5 Codes in the LCD-related Policy Article for applicable diagnoses)":
a beneficiary meets the humidification criteria
    if the medical record of the beneficiary documents thick tenacious secretions
    and the diagnosis of the beneficiary is in ICD10 group 5.

rule neb_ultrasonic_generator with provenance LCD L33370,
        confer "A small volume ultrasonic nebulizer (E0574) and related accessories are considered for coverage when it is reasonable and necessary to administer treprostinil inhalation solution to beneficiaries with pulmonary hypertension only":
a device meets the nebulizer coverage criteria
    if the HCPCS code of the device is "E0574"
    and the device administers covered treprostinil.

rule neb_administers_treprostinil with provenance LCD L33370,
        confer "Claims for code E0574 used with other inhalation solutions will be denied as not reasonable and necessary":
a device administers covered treprostinil
    if the device is furnished to a beneficiary
    and a drug is administered with the device
    and the HCPCS code of the drug is "J7686"
    and the drug is a covered inhalation drug for the beneficiary.

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% The accessories: covered with their related compressor, within the usual
% maximum replacement; the water and saline of the large volume nebulizer;
% the diluent of a concentrated drug.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

rule neb_accessory_claim with provenance LCD L33370,
        confer "Accessories are separately payable if the related aerosol compressor and the individual accessories are reasonable and necessary":
a claim is reasonable and necessary
    if the claim is for an item
    and the item is a nebulizer accessory
    and the item is an accessory of a device
    and the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the HCPCS code of the device is an other code
    and the related compressor of accessory the code is the other code under table nebulizer_related
    and the device meets the nebulizer coverage criteria
    and the claim is within the usual maximum replacement of the accessory.

rule neb_accessory_quantity with provenance LCD L33370,
        confer "Claims for more than the usual maximum replacement amount will be denied as not reasonable and necessary":
a claim is within the usual maximum replacement of the accessory
    if the claim is for an item
    and the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the usual maximum replacement for accessory the code is a quantity under table nebulizer_accessory_quantity
    and the period of the usual maximum replacement for accessory the code is a number months under table nebulizer_accessory_period
    and the claim is for a supply of an other number months
    and the quantity billed on the claim is a third number
    and a limit is the quantity * ceiling(the other number / the number)
    and the third number <= the limit.

rule neb_large_volume_water with provenance LCD L33370,
        confer "These codes are only reasonable and necessary when used in a large volume nebulizer (A7007, A7017, or E0585)":
a claim is reasonable and necessary
    if the claim is for an item
    and the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["A4217", "A7018"]
    and the item is an accessory of a device
    and the HCPCS code of the device is an other code
    and the other code is in ["A7007", "A7017", "E0585", "E0580"]
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the beneficiary meets the humidification criteria
    and the claim is within the usual maximum quantity per month.

rule neb_diluent with provenance LCD L33370,
        confer "separate saline solution (A4216 or A4218 [metered dose]) used to dilute it will be separately reimbursed":
a claim is reasonable and necessary
    if the claim is for an item
    and the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["A4216", "A4218"]
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and an other item is furnished to the beneficiary
    and the HCPCS code of the other item is an other code
    and the other code is in ["J7611", "J7612"]
    and the other item is a covered inhalation drug for the beneficiary
    and the claim is within the usual maximum quantity per month.

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% The inhalation drugs: covered for the diagnoses of their group, not
% together with a drug the LCD excludes them with, within the maximum per
% month.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

rule neb_drug_claim with provenance LCD L33370,
        confer "the coverage of such drugs or biologicals does not preclude the need for a determination that the drug or biological itself is reasonable and necessary for treatment of the illness or injury":
a claim is reasonable and necessary
    if the claim is for an item
    and the item is an inhalation drug
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the item is a covered inhalation drug for the beneficiary
    and it is not the case that
        the item conflicts with a concurrent inhalation drug
    and the claim is within the usual maximum quantity per month.

rule neb_drug_obstructive with provenance LCD L33370,
        confer "It is reasonable and necessary to administer albuterol (J7611, J7613), arformoterol (J7605), budesonide (J7626), cromolyn (J7631), formoterol (J7606), ipratropium (J7644), levalbuterol (J7612, J7614), metaproterenol (J7669), or revefenacin (J7677) for the management of obstructive pulmonary disease (refer to the Group 8 Codes in the LCD-related Policy Article for applicable diagnoses)":
an item is a covered inhalation drug for a beneficiary
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["J7611", "J7613", "J7605", "J7626", "J7631", "J7606", "J7644", "J7612", "J7614", "J7669", "J7677"]
    and the diagnosis of the beneficiary is in ICD10 group 8.

rule neb_drug_dornase_alfa with provenance LCD L33370,
        confer "It is reasonable and necessary to administer dornase alfa (J7639) to a beneficiary with cystic fibrosis (refer to the Group 9 Codes in the LCD-related Policy Article for applicable diagnoses)":
an item is a covered inhalation drug for a beneficiary
    if the HCPCS code of the item is "J7639"
    and the diagnosis of the beneficiary is in ICD10 group 9.

rule neb_drug_tobramycin with provenance LCD L33370,
        confer "It is reasonable and necessary to administer tobramycin (J7682) to a beneficiary with cystic fibrosis or bronchiectasis (refer to the Group 10 Codes in the LCD-related Policy Article for applicable diagnoses)":
an item is a covered inhalation drug for a beneficiary
    if the HCPCS code of the item is "J7682"
    and the diagnosis of the beneficiary is in ICD10 group 10.

rule neb_drug_pentamidine with provenance LCD L33370,
        confer "It is reasonable and necessary to administer pentamidine (J2545) to a beneficiary with HIV, pneumocystosis, or complications of organ transplants (refer to the Group 4 Codes in the LCD-related Policy Article for applicable diagnoses)":
an item is a covered inhalation drug for a beneficiary
    if the HCPCS code of the item is "J2545"
    and the diagnosis of the beneficiary is in ICD10 group 4.

rule neb_drug_acetylcysteine with provenance LCD L33370,
        confer "It is reasonable and necessary to administer acetylcysteine (J7608) for persistent thick or tenacious pulmonary secretions (refer to the Group 7 Codes in the LCD-related Policy Article for applicable diagnoses)":
an item is a covered inhalation drug for a beneficiary
    if the HCPCS code of the item is "J7608"
    and the diagnosis of the beneficiary is in ICD10 group 7.

rule neb_drug_hypertonic_saline with provenance LCD L33370,
        confer "It is reasonable and necessary to administer hypertonic saline (J7131) to a beneficiary with cystic fibrosis, bronchiectasis, or ciliary dyskinesia (refer to Group 15 Codes in the LCD-related Policy Article for applicable diagnoses)":
an item is a covered inhalation drug for a beneficiary
    if the HCPCS code of the item is "J7131"
    and the diagnosis of the beneficiary is in ICD10 group 15.

% Ensifentrine: an add-on to dual or triple maintenance therapy, for a
% beneficiary whose exacerbations continue or whose dyspnea persists.
rule neb_drug_ensifentrine with provenance LCD L33370,
        confer "It is reasonable and necessary to administer ensifentrine (J7601) as an add-on therapy for the management of chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (see Group 16 Codes in the LCD-related Policy Article)":
an item is a covered inhalation drug for a beneficiary
    if the HCPCS code of the item is "J7601"
    and the diagnosis of the beneficiary is in ICD10 group 16
    and the beneficiary meets the ensifentrine criteria.

rule neb_ensifentrine_criteria with provenance LCD L33370,
        confer "Use of ensifentrine (J7601) without either dual LABA/LAMA maintenance therapy or triple LABA/LAMA/ICS maintenance therapy will be considered not reasonable and necessary":
a beneficiary meets the ensifentrine criteria
    if the maintenance therapy of the beneficiary is a therapy
    and the therapy is in [dual long acting bronchodilator therapy, triple therapy with inhaled corticosteroid]
    and the finding maintenance therapy insufficient about the beneficiary is established.

% Treprostinil: pulmonary arterial hypertension (criteria 1–3) or pulmonary
% hypertension associated with interstitial lung disease (criterion 4).
rule neb_drug_treprostinil with provenance LCD L33370,
        confer "Treprostinil inhalation solution (J7686) is considered for coverage when either criteria 1-3; or , criterion 4 are met":
an item is a covered inhalation drug for a beneficiary
    if the HCPCS code of the item is "J7686"
    and the diagnosis of the beneficiary is in ICD10 group 11
    and the beneficiary meets the pulmonary arterial hypertension criteria.

rule neb_drug_treprostinil_ild with provenance LCD L33370,
        confer "The beneficiary has a diagnosis of pulmonary hypertension associated with interstitial lung disease (refer to Group 11 Codes in the LCD-related Policy Article for applicable diagnoses) and the following criteria (a-e) are met":
an item is a covered inhalation drug for a beneficiary
    if the HCPCS code of the item is "J7686"
    and the diagnosis of the beneficiary is in ICD10 group 11
    and the beneficiary meets the interstitial lung disease criteria.

rule neb_pah_criteria with provenance LCD L33370,
        confer "The beneficiary has primary pulmonary hypertension or pulmonary hypertension which is secondary to one of the following conditions: connective tissue disease, human immunodeficiency virus (HIV) infection, cirrhosis, anorexigens or congenital left to right shunts. If these conditions are present, the following criteria (a-d) must be met":
a beneficiary meets the pulmonary arterial hypertension criteria
    if the finding qualifying pulmonary hypertension etiology about the beneficiary is established
    and the finding pulmonary hypertension progressed despite treatment about the beneficiary is established
    and the mean pulmonary artery pressure of the beneficiary is elevated
    and the finding significant pulmonary hypertension symptoms about the beneficiary is established
    and the finding calcium channel blockers excluded about the beneficiary is established.

rule neb_mpap_at_rest with provenance LCD L33370,
        confer "The mean pulmonary artery pressure is > 25 mm Hg at rest or > 30 mm Hg with exertion":
the mean pulmonary artery pressure of a beneficiary is elevated
    if the mean pulmonary artery pressure of the beneficiary at rest is a number mm Hg
    and the number > 25.

rule neb_mpap_with_exertion with provenance LCD L33370,
        confer "The mean pulmonary artery pressure is > 25 mm Hg at rest or > 30 mm Hg with exertion":
the mean pulmonary artery pressure of a beneficiary is elevated
    if the mean pulmonary artery pressure of the beneficiary with exertion is a number mm Hg
    and the number > 30.

rule neb_ild_criteria with provenance LCD L33370,
        confer "The presence of interstitial lung disease has been confirmed by a high-resolution CT scan of the chest":
a beneficiary meets the interstitial lung disease criteria
    if interstitial lung disease of the beneficiary was confirmed by a high-resolution CT scan of the chest
    and the mean pulmonary artery pressure of the beneficiary at rest is a number mm Hg
    and the number >= 25
    and the filling pressure of the beneficiary is low
    and the pulmonary vascular resistance of the beneficiary at rest is an other number Wood units
    and the other number >= 3
    and the finding significant pulmonary hypertension symptoms about the beneficiary is established.

rule neb_wedge_pressure with provenance LCD L33370,
        confer "The pulmonary capillary wedge pressure or left ventricular end-diastolic pressure is ≤ 15mm Hg":
the filling pressure of a beneficiary is low
    if the pulmonary capillary wedge pressure of the beneficiary is a number mm Hg
    and the number <= 15.

rule neb_end_diastolic_pressure with provenance LCD L33370,
        confer "The pulmonary capillary wedge pressure or left ventricular end-diastolic pressure is ≤ 15mm Hg":
the filling pressure of a beneficiary is low
    if the left ventricular end-diastolic pressure of the beneficiary is a number mm Hg
    and the number <= 15.

% Drugs not used together: two short-acting beta agonists, two long-acting
% ones, ipratropium beside revefenacin, the components beside the J7620
% combination.
rule neb_one_short_acting with provenance LCD L33370,
        confer "Albuterol, levalbuterol, and metaproterenol are all short-acting bronchodilators with beta-adrenergic stimulatory effect. It is not reasonable and necessary for a beneficiary to use more than one of these at a time":
an item conflicts with a concurrent inhalation drug
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the usual maximum for code the code of drug a drug is a quantity units per month under table nebulizer_drug_max
    and the drug is in [albuterol, levalbuterol, metaproterenol]
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and an other item is furnished to the beneficiary
    and the HCPCS code of the other item is an other code
    and the usual maximum for code the other code of drug an other drug is an other quantity units per month under table nebulizer_drug_max
    and the other drug is in [albuterol, levalbuterol, metaproterenol]
    and the other drug is different from the drug.

rule neb_one_long_acting with provenance LCD L33370,
        confer "Formoterol and arformoterol are long-acting bronchodilators with beta-adrenergic stimulatory effect. It is not reasonable and necessary for a beneficiary to use more than one of these at a time":
an item conflicts with a concurrent inhalation drug
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the usual maximum for code the code of drug a drug is a quantity units per month under table nebulizer_drug_max
    and the drug is in [formoterol, arformoterol]
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and an other item is furnished to the beneficiary
    and the HCPCS code of the other item is an other code
    and the usual maximum for code the other code of drug an other drug is an other quantity units per month under table nebulizer_drug_max
    and the other drug is in [formoterol, arformoterol]
    and the other drug is different from the drug.

rule neb_ipratropium_with_revefenacin with provenance LCD L33370,
        confer "Concurrent use of long-acting and short-acting muscarinic antagonists, such as ipratropium (J7644) is not reasonable and necessary":
an item conflicts with a concurrent inhalation drug
    if the HCPCS code of the item is "J7644"
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and an other item is furnished to the beneficiary
    and the HCPCS code of the other item is "J7677".

rule neb_components_with_combination with provenance LCD L33370,
        confer "Claims for J7611, J7612, J7613, J7614, and J7644 billed in addition to J7620 will be denied as not reasonable and necessary":
an item conflicts with a concurrent inhalation drug
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["J7611", "J7612", "J7613", "J7614", "J7644"]
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and an other item is furnished to the beneficiary
    and the HCPCS code of the other item is "J7620".

% The maximum per month: the usual one, or the rescue one for a short-acting
% beta agonist beside formoterol or arformoterol, times the months supplied.
rule neb_usual_quantity with provenance LCD L33370,
        confer "Claims for more than these amounts of drugs will be denied as not reasonable and necessary":
a claim is within the usual maximum quantity per month
    if the claim is for an item
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and it is not the case that
        the item is a rescue medication for the beneficiary
    and the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the usual maximum for code the code of drug a drug is a quantity units per month under table nebulizer_drug_max
    and the claim is for a supply of a number months
    and the quantity billed on the claim is an other number
    and a limit is the quantity * the number
    and the other number <= the limit.

rule neb_rescue_quantity with provenance LCD L33370,
        confer "When albuterol, levalbuterol, or metaproterenol are prescribed as rescue/supplemental medication for beneficiaries who are taking formoterol or arformoterol, the maximum per month that are reasonably billed are":
a claim is within the usual maximum quantity per month
    if the claim is for an item
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the item is a rescue medication for the beneficiary
    and the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the rescue maximum for code the code is a quantity units per month under table nebulizer_rescue_max
    and the claim is for a supply of a number months
    and the quantity billed on the claim is an other number
    and a limit is the quantity * the number
    and the other number <= the limit.

% a drug with no stated maximum (tobramycin): any quantity ordered — a device
% of this model
rule neb_no_stated_maximum:
a claim is within the usual maximum quantity per month
    if the claim is for an item
    and the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and it is not the case that
        the usual maximum for code the code of drug a drug is a quantity units per month under table nebulizer_drug_max.

rule neb_rescue_medication with provenance LCD L33370,
        confer "Albuterol, levalbuterol, or metaproterenol is covered if it is used as a rescue/supplemental medication in addition to the long-acting beta-adrenergic agonist drug, formoterol or arformoterol":
an item is a rescue medication for a beneficiary
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the rescue maximum for code the code is a quantity units per month under table nebulizer_rescue_max
    and an other item is furnished to the beneficiary
    and the HCPCS code of the other item is an other code
    and the other code is in ["J7606", "J7605"].

section remedy is:

% The policy's own payment conditions: equipment has none (E0580: a
% beneficiary-owned oxygen system); a supply is dispensed for at most three
% months at a time, and ensifentrine needs the article's documentation.
rule neb_documentation_equipment with provenance Policy Article A52466,
        confer "Nebulizers are covered under the Durable Medical Equipment (DME) benefit":
the policy specific documentation requirements are met for a claim
    if the policy of the claim is nebulizers
    and the claim is for an item
    and the item is nebulizer equipment
    and it is not the case that
        the HCPCS code of the item is "E0580".

rule neb_documentation_bottle_nebulizer with provenance Policy Article A52466,
        confer "should only be billed when this type of nebulizer is used with a beneficiary-owned oxygen system":
the policy specific documentation requirements are met for a claim
    if the policy of the claim is nebulizers
    and the claim is for an item
    and the HCPCS code of the item is "E0580"
    and the item is used with a patient owned oxygen system.

rule neb_dispensing_limit with provenance LCD L33370,
        confer "Regardless of utilization, a supplier must not dispense more than a three (3) - month quantity at a time":
the policy specific documentation requirements are met for a claim
    if the policy of the claim is nebulizers
    and the claim is for an item
    and the item is a nebulizer supply
    and the claim is for a supply of a number months
    and the number <= 3
    and the ensifentrine documentation requirements are met for the claim.

rule neb_ensifentrine_documentation with provenance Policy Article A52466,
        confer "the treating practitioner must document in the beneficiary’s medical records 1 and either 2 or 3 below":
the ensifentrine documentation requirements are met for a claim
    if the claim is for an item
    and the HCPCS code of the item is "J7601"
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the medical record of the beneficiary documents continued maintenance therapy
    and the medical record of the beneficiary documents a condition
    and the condition is in [continued COPD exacerbations, persistent COPD related dyspnea].

% any other supply: no documentation of its own — a device of this model
rule neb_ensifentrine_documentation_not_needed:
the ensifentrine documentation requirements are met for a claim
    if the claim is for an item
    and it is not the case that
        the HCPCS code of the item is "J7601".
